Today is Monday.
Now it is evening.
My work finishes at five o'clock every day.
I go outside with my bicycle.
I walk to a small repair shop.
This shop is near my apartment.
A mechanic is there.
I say hello to him.
"Namaskaram," he replies.
"This bicycle needs a service," I say.
He looks at the bicycle.
"Okay, I will do it," the mechanic says.
"At what time will you come?" he asks.
"I will come on Wednesday," I say.
"At what time on Wednesday?" he asks.
"I will come at seven o'clock in the evening," I say.
"Okay, come at seven o'clock," he says.
I leave the bicycle at the shop.
After that, I walk back home.
